title: Config `defines` replaces the game-target defines instead of adding to them
updated_at: "2026-08-29T04:35:24Z"
---
Reported by Max, 2026-08-29, from ~/src/openplanet/my-plugins/tm-editor-plus-plus.

## Symptom
`.openplanet-lsp.toml` containing `defines = ["DEV"]` leaves the analysis with
EXACTLY `{DEV}`: TMNEXT, WINDOWS, MANIA64, SIG_* and every other target-derived
define disappear. Every `#if TMNEXT` branch in the plugin goes dead, so real
code is masked out and floods undefined-identifier false positives.

## Cause
src/config.rs `apply_config_file` / `apply_init_options` do
`self.defines = defines.into_iter().collect(); self.defines_overridden = true;`
— a whole-set replace — and `load_with_parent` then SKIPS the
`defines_for_target(game_target)` re-derivation whenever `defines_overridden`
is set (added for GH #36).

## Expected
A user's custom defines are ADDITIVE on top of the target-derived set. Turning
a define OFF needs an explicit opt-out (`-NAME` / `!NAME`), not a silent wipe.
A platform selector listed by hand (e.g. `defines = ["MP4"]` while the target
is TMNEXT) must still leave exactly one platform family live — GH #36's
invariant.

## Second, smaller item (same report)
The config TUI's `defines` row gives no format hint: nothing says the editor
takes a comma-separated list, and there is no example. Same for the other
StringList keys.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Red: workspace `.openplanet-lsp.toml` with `defines = ["DEV"]` -> config.defines
contains DEV **and** TMNEXT + WINDOWS. Variants: init options; user-global file;
parent + per-root accumulation in a multi-root workspace; `game_target = "TURBO"`
plus `defines = ["DEV"]` -> TURBO kept, TMNEXT absent; `-TMNEXT` / `!LOGS`
removal; `defines = ["MP4"]` under a TMNEXT target -> MP4 live, TMNEXT dead;
manifest `[script].defines` still additive and a `-NAME` still wins over it.